ry | `#FFFFFF` | `--color-on-primary` |\n| Secondary | `#334155` | `--color-secondary` |\n| On Secondary | `#FFFFFF` | `--color-on-secondary` |\n| Accent/CTA | `#DC2626` | `--color-accent` |\n| On Accent/CTA | `#FFFFFF` | `--color-on-accent` |\n| Background | `#F8FAFC` | `--color-background` |\n| Foreground | `#0F172A` | `--color-foreground` |\n| Card | `#FFFFFF` | `--color-card` |\n| Card Foreground | `#0F172A` | `--color-card-foreground` |\n| Muted | `#E9EDF1` | `--color-muted` |\n| Muted Foreground | `#475569` | `--color-muted-foreground` |\n| Border | `#E2E8F0` | `--color-border` |\n| Destructive | `#DC2626` | `--color-destructive` |\n| On Destructive | `#FFFFFF` | `--color-on-destructive` |\n| Ring | `#1E293B` | `--color-ring` |\n\n*Notes: Premium dark + action red*\n\n### Typography\n- **Heading:** Syncopate\n- **Body:** Space Mono\n- **Mood:** kinetic, motion, futuristic, speed, wide, tech\n- **Best For:** Music festivals, automotive, high-energy brands\n- **Google Fonts:** https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Mono:wght@400;700&family=Syncopate:wght@400;700&display=swap\n- **CSS Import:**\n```css\n@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Mono:wght@400;700&family=Syncopate:wght@400;700&display=swap');\n```\n\n### Key Effects\nScroll anim (Intersection Observer), hover (300-400ms), entrance, parallax (3-5 layers), page transitions\n\n### Avoid (Anti-patterns)\n- Static product pages\n- Poor UX\n\n### Pre-Delivery Checklist\n- [ ] No emojis as icons (use SVG: Heroicons/Lucide)\n- [ ] cursor-pointer on all clickable elements\n- [ ] Hover states with smooth transitions (150-300ms)\n- [ ] Light mode: text contrast 4.5:1 minimum\n- [ ] Focus states visible for keyboard nav\n- [ ] prefers-reduced-motion respected\n- [ ] Responsive: 375px, 768px, 1024px, 1440px\n\nLooks of the most recent other projects (newest first, then older ones in this product's field). This product must not look like any of them:\n1. [devtools+hr] #356F9A light, auto frame, sans type, soft corners, flat surfaces, hero none, soft charts, mixed pictures, cool greys, plain bar, glyph mark (\"Sign-in begins at S-1. Google OAuth retu\")\n2. [devtools+automotive] #1F6F5C light, auto frame, sans type, soft corners, flat surfaces, hero none, soft charts, mixed pictures, cool greys, plain bar, glyph mark (\"Sign-in with Folio3 Google Workspace (S-\")\n3. #176B5E light, topbar frame, humanist+slab type, sharp corners, flat surfaces, hero none, mono charts, icons pictures, cool greys, plain bar, glyph mark (\"steady operational\")\n4. [travel] #232A4E auto, topbar frame, grotesk+condensed type, round corners, soft surfaces, hero none, bold charts, icons pictures, warm greys, plain bar, wordmark mark (\"Boutique energetic, warm and round\")\n5. [retail] #1E4BB8 light, topbar frame, sans+slab type, soft corners, flat surfaces, hero none, mono charts, icons pictures, cool greys, plain bar, emblem mark (\"Trade-counter precise: compact, cool\")\n1 of them is in this product's own field (insurance+automotive). Those took the field's obvious looks first, so this one must find what makes THIS product different from them, from its own users and requirements, rather than the field's next-most-obvious look.\nDiffer from each in at least 4 points (a different colour family counts 2; each of mode, frame, type, corners, surfaces, hero, charts, pictures, greys, bar and mark counts 1; type is the body and heading pair). Let the product reading decide where to differ, not chance.\n\n<artifact id=\"requirements\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall authenticate employees only through Folio3 Google Workspace accounts and reject personal Gmail accounts and other non-Folio3 identities.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n  \"ears\": \"When an employee signs in, the Folio3 parking web app shall require the signed-in Folio3 Google identity to match the corporate email used for that employee's self-service profile lookup, restrict employee and vehicle data to that employee, and permit administrators to access other employee records only under their authorized permissions, while retrieving employee identity from the corporate directory and parking assignments and registered vehicle details from the administrator-maintained roster initially loaded from existing records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n  \"ears\": \"If an employee without dedicated parking has no registered vehicle, then the Folio3 parking web app shall require registration of at least one license plate before enabling claims, permit one or more registered plates with optional make, model, and color, and activate each newly registered plate immediately.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall treat Monday through Friday as working days, including holidays, when applying default dedicated-parking availability and utilization scenarios.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n  \"ears\": \"If a dedicated parking holder releases today's assigned space, then the Folio3 parking web app shall accept the release in one action, reject a duplicate release for that date, and expose the space status as Reserved, Released, or Claimed.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall allow dedicated parking holders to schedule one or more parking releases on dates up to 30 calendar days ahead and display saved releases on a calendar.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall allow a dedicated parking holder to cancel a scheduled release only while that date's space has not been claimed and record each scheduling and cancellation event.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall use 8:00 AM as the default daily parking release time and allow an administrator to configure that time in the office's local timezone.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall evaluate today, the 30-day scheduling window, daily release cutoffs, and weekly report scheduling using the configured office-local timezone.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n  \"ears\": \"When a scheduled release reaches the daily release time or a same-day release occurs, the Folio3 parking web app shall make the space claimable at the daily release time for scheduled releases and same-day releases before that time, and immediately for same-day releases after that time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall provide available-space counts and allocate each available space to the first eligible non-dedicated employee whose claim is accepted, allowing each space to be claimed only once.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall require an employee claiming temporary parking to select one registered vehicle, authorize only that vehicle's plate for the allocation, and assign a floor with the most remaining capacity using a consistent tie-break when floors have equal remaining capacity.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n  \"ears\": \"When one or more parking spaces become available, the Folio3 parking web app shall send an email notification using a fixed template to eligible employees without dedicated parking.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall reject employee cancellation of a temporary parking claim in Phase 1.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-15\",\n  \"ears\": \"When the existing entrance LPR camera reports a car plate detection, the Folio3 parking web app shall verify the plate against an active temporary allocation for the office-local date, request green-indicator activation only for valid authorization, and record the attempt's date, time, plate, verification result, and entry status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-16\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall record permanent-sticker vehicle plate detections for utilization, bypass temporary authorization and entry blocking for those vehicles, and, when a permanent holder enters a released space allocated temporarily, cancel that temporary allocation so subsequent verification denies the temporary claimant authorization for that space.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-17\",\n  \"ears\": \"If the camera, plate recognition, network, or indicator fails or a plate cannot be read during an entrance check, then the Folio3 parking web app shall record an unsuccessful verification, keep green authorization off, and deny entry until service is restored without offering a manual-verification path.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-18\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall record an Unused Dedicated Parking event for each working day when a dedicated holder did not release the space and no registered vehicle entry was detected, and an Unused Temporary Parking event when a claimant's selected vehicle was not detected entering on the claim date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-19\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall generate a weekly utilization report every Monday morning in the office timezone containing dedicated employees who neither released nor used their parking, temporary claimants who did not use their parking, daily and weekly utilization statistics, total released spaces, total temporary claims, and an overall utilization percentage.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-20\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall email each weekly utilization report to the designated stakeholders using the configured stakeholder recipient list and permit only authenticated parking administrators to update that list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-21\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall not create automated warnings, suspensions, or penalties based on parking utilization in Phase 1.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-22\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking web app shall retain release, claim, LPR verification, and utilization history according to Folio3's existing records-retention policy.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nDraw the screen inventory."}